1
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:30,520
You're just afraid your guy will lose,
so you want me to throw.

2
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,840
I already gave you a chance.

3
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:36,440
Arm!

4
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:40,520
If I lived at a boxing camp,
I wouldn't get to be with you.

5
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:43,000
That's why you just keep living off her.

6
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:44,160
Transfer where?

7
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:45,480
Bangkok.

8
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:47,000
Khon Kaen? I'm not going.

9
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:48,080
This guy

10
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:50,240
<i>has never lost a fight.</i>

11
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,480
Are you moving to Bangkok together?

12
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:57,080
Your dad already thinks
I'm living off you.

13
00:01:57,160 --> 00:02:00,160
If I go there without a job,
he'll think even worse.

14
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:03,040
You'll have to work for me.
Go undercover and join Oab's group.

15
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:04,520
<i>If you solve this case,</i>

16
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:07,520
<i>I'll make you a police-affiliated boxer.</i>

17
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:10,880
<i>You need to get evidence to arrest Oab.</i>
<i>Proof he's trafficking drugs.</i>

18
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:14,080
-Dom, stay and watch the bar tonight.
-Yes.

19
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:17,680
-I'll sleep here with you.
-Looks like I won't be sleeping.

20
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:21,120
Dum. Dom!

21
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:23,400
Hey, Dom!

22
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,520
Come with me.

23
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:33,880
Yes.

24
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:40,760
Good!

25
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:44,600
One, two.

26
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:47,520
Here, come this way.

27
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:49,760
Good!

28
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:51,480
Come on.

29
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,720
-Step back.
-Hello.

30
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:58,720
Hey, spar with me for a round.

31
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:01,880
You're gonna fight, Oab?

32
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:02,960
Yeah.

33
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:06,600
Dum, is Oab putting me in the ring?

34
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:08,880
Yeah.

35
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:14,120
Didn't you hear what I said?

36
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:15,760
Yes.

37
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,080
What's up with him?

38
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:22,080
Maybe he just wants some exercise.

39
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:25,640
But I haven't seen him spar
in a long time.

40
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:30,200
Not since what happened with Arm.

41
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:35,200
Or maybe he wants to push Dom?

42
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:56,560
Maybe he's not home.

43
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,800
Hello?

44
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:08,960
<i>Mom.</i>

45
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:09,960
Oh.

46
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,240
How are you, dear?

47
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:12,920
I'm fine.

48
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:16,640
Mom, have you seen Dom?

49
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:18,360
<i>He's not answering my calls.</i>

50
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,440
You're going to Bangkok?

51
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:24,360
Yes, Mom.

52
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:26,120
To follow Fon?

53
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,160
Does she know you're going?

54
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:32,720
I haven't told her yet, Mom.

55
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:36,280
That's why I wanted to ask you.

56
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,680
I want to keep it a secret for now
that I'm going to Bangkok.

57
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:43,280
I won't stop you

58
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:45,800
if what you're doing is for the best.

59
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:51,800
But remember,
there's no such thing as a secret forever.

60
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,480
I think he's probably training right now.

61
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:04,400
I'll tell him to call you back.

62
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:06,880
Okay.

63
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:15,280
They still haven't seen each other?

64
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:18,600
What are you up to, Dom?

65
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,960
NO GAMBLING

66
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:06,800
Look at that!

67
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,640
That's enough for today.

68
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:21,280
He's actually a pretty good fighter.

69
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:23,560
I think Oab might like Dom.

70
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:27,400
Wait here for me.
I have a job for you tonight.

71
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:29,240
Here we go.

72
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:39,760
Dum.

73
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:41,960
Is he giving me
another job like last night?

74
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:44,080
Kill someone?

75
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:45,520
Maybe.

76
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:56,280
MAN OCEAN VS KAEN NARASINGH, 25 MARCH 1990

77
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:07,080
That kid wasn't any good
when we saw him fight, was he?

78
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:10,000
You still want to push him?
Is he really gonna make it?

79
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:14,000
I don't think he's that bad.

80
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,240
Yeah.

81
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,960
I think he's got good form.

82
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:19,840
We should put some work into him.
If he makes it,

83
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:22,080
our camp gets another shot.

84
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:35,640
<i>Stand by.</i>

85
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:38,200
Move in!

86
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:41,960
Stop!

87
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,040
Hey, get down!

88
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,080
Hey, bro!

89
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:25,440
-Watch out!
-Take this!

90
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:44,720
Go!

91
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:48,560
Hey!

92
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:53,280
Hey!

93
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:14,840
CRIME SUPPRESSION

94
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:26,800
<i>Are they really selling drugs?</i>

95
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:31,120
<i>It's just boxers and gangsters here.</i>

96
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:36,360
<i>I need to find proof</i>
<i>they have drugs in their possession.</i>

97
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:39,040
<i>How am I gonna ditch these two?</i>

98
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:43,080
No more moves.

99
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:44,200
Pong.

100
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:45,680
Someone got caught delivering drugs.

101
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:49,240
Really?

102
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:52,080
Confirmed just now.
It was a big shipment too.

103
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:54,000
Thanks.

104
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,480
Dum.

105
00:09:58,360 --> 00:10:00,120
-What happened?
-None of your business.

106
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:06,360
Did one of Oab's men get arrested?

107
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:27,920
-Hey!
-Whoa!

108
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,240
Who the hell are you?

109
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:30,200
Hey!

110
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:32,560
Hey, your ass! How'd you get in here?

111
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:34,200
Uh…

112
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:39,040
Well, I couldn't find the bathroom.

113
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:40,080
The bathroom?

114
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:41,760
Nice excuse.

115
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:45,600
I'm not making excuses.
I work with Dum at the bar.

116
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:48,960
Dum?

117
00:11:51,040 --> 00:11:52,040
You're the new guy?

118
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:53,920
Yes.

119
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:02,360
-What's your name?
-Dom.

120
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:05,480
I'm Haw.

121
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:08,400
Come on, I'll show you the bathroom.

122
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:10,200
You know who I am?

123
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,960
How do you know Dum but not me?

124
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:15,280
Everyone here knows me.

125
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:17,120
-Didn't he ever mention me?
-No.

126
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:19,320
If you need anything here, just ask me.

127
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:25,200
If you need anything, just tell me.

128
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:28,320
I've been here longer than you,
maybe I can help you, bro.

129
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:29,880
-Thank you.
-No problem.

130
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:31,480
Ouch!

131
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:34,240
Haw, damn you!

132
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:38,000
I've been looking for you all day.
Where the hell were you this morning?

133
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:39,680
Aren't you supposed to be cleaning?

134
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,960
Huh?

135
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:43,360
Yes.

136
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:46,560
Yeah. You've only been here a few days
and you're already slacking off.

137
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:48,080
A few days?

138
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:49,520
Yeah.

139
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:51,360
He only started
two or three days before you.

140
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:53,280
Go on. Clean this place up.

141
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:56,920
-Do it right, or you're in trouble.
-Yes.

142
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:03,320
"If you need anything, just tell me.
I've been here longer." Hah!

143
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:04,960
Three days.

144
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:07,200
Three days still counts, right?

145
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,320
No, it doesn't.

146
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:11,080
Fine, it doesn't count.

147
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:22,280
Hey, Dom.

148
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:23,440
-Huh?
-Here.

149
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:27,520
You made me sweep,
and now you want me to mop too?

150
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:29,320
Yeah.

151
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:31,520
You have to wait for him anyway.

152
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:33,800
You'll be done mopping
by the time he leaves.

153
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,320
Over there.

154
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:55,440
Hey, Haw.

155
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:56,360
Yeah?

156
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:58,240
What does Oab do?

157
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:01,600
Mostly construction,

158
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:04,480
a few bars, a gambling den,

159
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,880
and this boxing camp.

160
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:11,320
That's it?

161
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:15,160
That's already a lot.
That's how he can afford to run this camp.

162
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:21,000
What? Why do you look so disappointed?

163
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:23,080
No, nothing.

164
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:25,320
Why do you care so much?

165
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:27,920
He hired you.
As long as you're paid, that's enough.

166
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:29,600
Now keep mopping.

167
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:36,920
Damn it! I pay that bastard every month.

168
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,400
And he still seized my goods?
Have you called him yet?

169
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,080
He said he did it to boost his record.

170
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:45,680
Record? Here's your record!

171
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:47,680
He should've told me first.

172
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:51,560
I could've set up a small batch for him.
Instead, he took down my big one.

173
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:53,320
Damn it!

174
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:55,480
Who the hell tipped him off?

175
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:59,720
If they find out you tipped them off,
they'll come after you.

176
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,440
I'm not worried.

177
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:04,400
But their network is huge.
If you expose them

178
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:07,560
and they all come after us,
we won't stand a chance.

179
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:10,560
Are you scared?

180
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:12,840
You guys

181
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:15,840
are all I have. If you're in, I'm in.

182
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:36,320
Why are you so damn curious?

183
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:42,400
He has so many businesses.
How does he manage them all?

184
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:44,960
He invests,

185
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:48,280
then lets his people run them.
The profits are split fairly.

186
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:53,320
Do you think there are drugs involved?

187
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:57,240
Watch your mouth.

188
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:00,840
No, I'm asking because…

189
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:03,720
if there is, I'm out.
I don't wanna end up in jail.

190
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,320
Oh.

191
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:08,760
I don't know. I'm new here, just like you.

192
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:22,640
KING BOXING CAMP

193
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:42,560
Sir, I'm at the boxing camp now.

194
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:57,480
-Who were you calling?
-My mom.

195
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:14,359
Hey, come help me out.

196
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:15,560
-Yeah.
-Here.

197
00:17:16,079 --> 00:17:17,319
There's a ton of work.

198
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:20,040
Thanks, coach. I'll leave it to you.

199
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:21,760
Dum.

200
00:17:21,839 --> 00:17:23,200
I don't trust this guy.

201
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:25,880
Are you overthinking it?

202
00:17:26,839 --> 00:17:28,520
I've never seen you trust anyone.

203
00:17:29,160 --> 00:17:31,760
This bastard really can't be trusted.

204
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:39,080
-Are we gonna get it done?
-Pong!

205
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:40,320
The wreaths.

206
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:42,840
Please put them in the car.

207
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:49,760
Hey, Haw. Do you know
whose funeral he's going to?

208
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:52,440
I've been sitting here with you.
How would I know?

209
00:17:55,520 --> 00:17:57,280
Dum, you know?

210
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:10,080
You bring this for your mother or what?

211
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:14,040
I heard you took a big hit,
so I brought flowers to pay my respects.

212
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:16,760
Are you messing with me? Huh?

213
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:22,160
There are a lot of witnesses.

214
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,360
You sure?

215
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:35,520
Hello.

216
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:37,480
Uh…

217
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:39,160
Is there a problem here?

218
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:41,600
Hello, officer.

219
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,720
No, it's nothing.

220
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:50,560
I just stopped by
to say hi to an old friend.

221
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:55,560
Alright, I'll be leaving.

222
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:21,800
Dum did a good job.

223
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,520
Damn mosquitoes.

224
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:04,760
Ready?

225
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:06,160
Um…

226
00:20:09,280 --> 00:20:10,160
Give Dom the keys.

227
00:20:15,520 --> 00:20:16,560
You drive.

228
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:19,680
You go home first.

229
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:24,880
You're going with him alone?
Let me go with you.

230
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:27,480
It's fine. I can handle it. Don't worry.

231
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:29,520
Come on, Dom.

232
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:44,880
Hey.

233
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:46,840
You're not going with Oab?

234
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:50,320
Who knows what he's thinking?

235
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:54,560
Let's have a beer.

236
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:11,880
You got this! Keep it up!

237
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:13,160
Come on!

238
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:17,000
Harder! Yeah!

239
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,520
You're up after this fight.

240
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:45,040
Is that guy one of Pom's men?

241
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:47,480
Yeah. That guy's damn unlucky.

242
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:49,400
First fight here,
and he gets one of Pom's guys.

243
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:01,160
Street fights…

244
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:04,240
No rules, no regulations.

245
00:22:05,520 --> 00:22:06,840
Last one standing wins.

246
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:19,760
Go for it!

247
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:20,720
Fight!

248
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:22,560
Get him! Come on!

249
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:24,560
-Finish him!
-Yeah!

250
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:45,080
That's it!

251
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:56,400
He won!

252
00:24:30,040 --> 00:24:31,080
Hey!

253
00:24:32,440 --> 00:24:33,520
You're still coming back?

254
00:24:37,080 --> 00:24:40,240
Arm's already dead.
I think you should shut the camp down.

255
00:24:41,040 --> 00:24:44,880
Stop trying.
You guys will never take down Ocean Camp.

256
00:24:46,280 --> 00:24:48,000
This is who you got?

257
00:24:53,640 --> 00:24:54,920
Get in the car.

258
00:25:03,200 --> 00:25:04,200
Hey.

259
00:25:04,800 --> 00:25:07,680
New guy,
you're not even gonna show some respect?

260
00:25:27,640 --> 00:25:28,640
You guys asked for this.

261
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:44,480
Didn't Peng tell you?
No fighting around here.

262
00:25:50,400 --> 00:25:51,400
You okay?

263
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:17,480
Why did you let them make the first move?

264
00:26:17,560 --> 00:26:20,760
If we started it,
we'd be banned from fighting there.

265
00:26:24,440 --> 00:26:26,280
Don't go to work tomorrow.

266
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:29,920
Why? Are you kicking me out?

267
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:31,000
Ugh.

268
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:33,720
Look at yourself. Get some rest.

269
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:35,640
Go back the day after tomorrow.

270
00:26:36,680 --> 00:26:39,760
From now on, sleep at the boxing camp.

271
00:26:40,680 --> 00:26:41,800
No more bar duty.

272
00:26:45,920 --> 00:26:46,840
Thank you, Boss.

273
00:26:56,440 --> 00:26:57,440
Haw.

274
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:03,560
Haw! Dom's here.

275
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Yes.

276
00:27:06,080 --> 00:27:08,800
You two sleep in the same room.
Your bag is over there.

277
00:27:08,880 --> 00:27:11,480
I'm in the room next door.
Call me if you need anything.

278
00:27:12,520 --> 00:27:13,600
Dum.

279
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:17,120
-Thank you.
-Yeah.

280
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:19,800
Hey.

281
00:27:20,400 --> 00:27:21,760
Do you snore?

282
00:27:22,600 --> 00:27:23,440
No.

283
00:27:23,520 --> 00:27:26,720
Good. I can't sleep with loud snoring.

284
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:45,600
<i>Sir.</i>

285
00:27:45,680 --> 00:27:46,960
I need your help.

286
00:27:47,480 --> 00:27:49,480
Tonight, Oab is taking me somewhere.

287
00:27:51,240 --> 00:27:54,400
I need him to trust me. I have a plan,

288
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:57,320
but I need your help.

289
00:28:10,440 --> 00:28:11,880
Boss, I'll have…

290
00:28:12,680 --> 00:28:14,920
one stewed pork rice, add an egg.
Chrysanthemum drink too.

291
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:15,800
Hey.

292
00:28:17,520 --> 00:28:19,120
I heard some thugs jumped you last night?

293
00:28:20,880 --> 00:28:22,600
-Yeah.
-See?

294
00:28:22,680 --> 00:28:24,600
I wanted to go with you,
but you wouldn't let me.

295
00:28:25,440 --> 00:28:27,800
That new guy must've tipped them off.

296
00:28:29,280 --> 00:28:30,600
Who do those thugs work for?

297
00:28:32,120 --> 00:28:33,320
It was Peng.

298
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:38,560
I went to see him yesterday.
He was mad, but couldn't do anything.

299
00:28:39,320 --> 00:28:41,040
So he sent his guys after me.

300
00:28:41,800 --> 00:28:43,160
You need to chill, Oab.

301
00:28:43,240 --> 00:28:45,320
-No.
-What?

302
00:28:45,400 --> 00:28:47,600
I'm joking. Yeah, I know.

303
00:28:49,120 --> 00:28:50,800
I think Peng has someone backing him.

304
00:28:55,600 --> 00:28:56,600
<i>Last night,</i>

305
00:28:57,720 --> 00:28:59,600
<i>I saw people using drugs at his bar.</i>

306
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:05,280
Why couldn't you just arrest them?

307
00:29:05,840 --> 00:29:07,480
The evidence was right there in his bar.

308
00:29:09,480 --> 00:29:11,280
I think we need to find out
who's backing him.

309
00:29:12,040 --> 00:29:14,280
If I rush in blindly, I'll lose my badge.

310
00:29:15,320 --> 00:29:16,240
So you can't do anything.

311
00:29:16,920 --> 00:29:18,360
It means you guys have to wait.

312
00:29:20,480 --> 00:29:22,440
So you're getting back into boxing?

313
00:29:23,320 --> 00:29:24,480
Yeah.

314
00:29:25,440 --> 00:29:28,200
I was really happy to see you last night.

315
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:31,560
I thought you'd given up.

316
00:29:32,160 --> 00:29:33,800
But I knew you'd never quit.

317
00:29:34,480 --> 00:29:35,400
Yeah.

318
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:37,840
You and Arm have
been boxing since you were kids.

319
00:29:37,920 --> 00:29:40,280
Right punch.
Yeah, like that. Keep punching.

320
00:29:40,360 --> 00:29:41,360
Yeah.

321
00:29:41,440 --> 00:29:42,480
Good.

322
00:29:42,560 --> 00:29:43,520
Yes!

323
00:29:43,600 --> 00:29:44,920
Keep going.

324
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:47,480
Oab! Arm! Some kids are beating up Pong.

325
00:29:47,560 --> 00:29:48,720
-Hurry!
-What? Let's go!

326
00:29:59,320 --> 00:30:00,840
Get up!

327
00:30:31,720 --> 00:30:33,360
Thanks, guys.

328
00:30:33,880 --> 00:30:34,800
I remember that day.

329
00:30:34,880 --> 00:30:37,360
I would've died
if you guys hadn't helped me.

330
00:30:44,640 --> 00:30:45,520
Oab.

331
00:30:46,920 --> 00:30:49,440
You came back
because of that kid last night, right?

332
00:30:51,640 --> 00:30:53,280
I saw him fight just like Arm.

333
00:30:55,080 --> 00:30:56,680
I don't think we can trust him.

334
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:01,440
-Why?
-When he started working here,

335
00:31:01,520 --> 00:31:03,840
Peng's men were waiting outside the bar.

336
00:31:05,120 --> 00:31:06,360
Not to mention last night.

337
00:31:06,960 --> 00:31:10,360
When Oab ordered him
to shoot Peng's man, he didn't.

338
00:31:13,400 --> 00:31:16,280
Maybe he's just new.
Shooting someone isn't easy.

339
00:31:20,440 --> 00:31:21,320
I need your help.

340
00:31:22,680 --> 00:31:23,680
With what?

341
00:31:23,760 --> 00:31:25,720
Look into someone's background for me.

342
00:31:28,480 --> 00:31:29,480
Whose background?

343
00:31:41,240 --> 00:31:42,320
Fon.

344
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:47,160
Dom?

345
00:31:58,600 --> 00:31:59,680
How did you get here?

346
00:32:02,040 --> 00:32:03,320
And what happened to you?

347
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:06,560
Boxing.

348
00:32:07,440 --> 00:32:08,840
There's a temple fair again?

349
00:32:09,520 --> 00:32:10,480
Yeah.

350
00:32:13,680 --> 00:32:17,200
Who did you fight?
Why are you this badly hurt?

351
00:32:21,800 --> 00:32:23,480
Let's put some medicine on it.

352
00:32:38,320 --> 00:32:39,240
Oh no.

353
00:32:40,280 --> 00:32:41,520
You're pretty bruised up.

354
00:32:49,880 --> 00:32:50,920
Does it hurt?

355
00:33:03,400 --> 00:33:05,800
Why didn't you tell me you were coming?

356
00:33:08,440 --> 00:33:09,560
I wanted to surprise you.

357
00:33:17,560 --> 00:33:18,680
How long are you staying?

358
00:33:20,360 --> 00:33:22,080
Probably just one day.

359
00:33:23,480 --> 00:33:24,600
Why?

360
00:33:26,040 --> 00:33:28,560
Can't you stay two or three days?

361
00:33:29,200 --> 00:33:30,520
I miss you.

362
00:33:50,280 --> 00:33:51,680
I miss you too.

363
00:34:27,719 --> 00:34:30,159
Do you know how many times I called you?

364
00:34:37,400 --> 00:34:38,400
I'm sorry.

365
00:34:40,760 --> 00:34:41,760
Yeah.

366
00:34:50,920 --> 00:34:52,120
Trust me.

367
00:34:52,840 --> 00:34:54,960
I promise I'll never hurt you.

368
00:35:02,640 --> 00:35:03,480
Really?

369
00:35:07,640 --> 00:35:08,760
Really.

370
00:35:25,960 --> 00:35:28,680
Why only one day? You came all this way.

371
00:35:29,440 --> 00:35:30,600
I got a job.

372
00:35:30,680 --> 00:35:32,880
Wait, really?

373
00:35:32,960 --> 00:35:34,120
Where, Dom?

374
00:35:34,200 --> 00:35:35,680
At a small bar.

375
00:35:37,440 --> 00:35:38,640
Wait.

376
00:35:38,720 --> 00:35:41,640
If you have a job now,
you can stay longer, right?

377
00:35:41,720 --> 00:35:43,240
Why are you only staying one day?

378
00:35:45,240 --> 00:35:46,400
I have to work.

379
00:35:49,240 --> 00:35:50,440
Then…

380
00:35:50,520 --> 00:35:53,640
I'll look for a place to rent.
We can move in together.

381
00:35:53,720 --> 00:35:57,200
My boss already has a place for me.
Everyone stays there.

382
00:35:57,960 --> 00:35:59,800
Then I'll move in with you.

383
00:36:01,400 --> 00:36:04,080
You can't. I already have a roommate.

384
00:36:05,680 --> 00:36:08,680
And everyone there is a guy.

385
00:36:12,080 --> 00:36:14,000
Why is everything impossible?

386
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:17,760
I'm sorry.

387
00:36:23,960 --> 00:36:25,560
I really understand, Dom.

388
00:36:26,440 --> 00:36:27,720
You don't have to apologize.

389
00:36:28,880 --> 00:36:30,720
You already moved here for me.

390
00:36:34,160 --> 00:36:36,360
Let's wait until things settle down.

391
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:38,520
Then we'll find a way to live together.

392
00:36:39,080 --> 00:36:42,320
For now, we can just meet on our days off.
Is that okay?

393
00:36:49,320 --> 00:36:52,120
I'll come see you after work sometime.

394
00:36:53,120 --> 00:36:54,280
Okay?

395
00:36:54,360 --> 00:36:55,520
Better not, Fon.

396
00:36:56,480 --> 00:36:57,320
What?

397
00:36:57,920 --> 00:36:58,760
Why?

398
00:36:59,920 --> 00:37:02,080
Dom, you're acting strange.

399
00:37:02,680 --> 00:37:07,080
I can't move in. You can't stay with me.
Now I can't even see you?

400
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:22,760
That's Dom.

401
00:37:26,760 --> 00:37:27,840
Who's he meeting?

402
00:37:33,880 --> 00:37:37,720
Dom, do you have someone else?

403
00:37:39,480 --> 00:37:40,480
Dom.

404
00:37:52,120 --> 00:37:53,000
Fon?

405
00:37:54,680 --> 00:37:55,680
Oab?

406
00:38:18,600 --> 00:38:20,600
I thought you wouldn't make it in time.

407
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:23,120
What happened?

408
00:38:25,080 --> 00:38:26,200
Mom…

409
00:38:29,640 --> 00:38:31,400
Let's go. We need to leave.

410
00:38:32,120 --> 00:38:33,160
Yes.

411
00:38:47,880 --> 00:38:50,000
Fon, are you breaking up with me?

412
00:38:52,760 --> 00:38:54,200
So you won't forget me.

413
00:38:58,360 --> 00:39:02,240
<i>I promise,</i>
<i>when I'm ready, I'll come back to you.</i>

414
00:39:08,160 --> 00:39:09,080
This is…

415
00:39:10,600 --> 00:39:11,880
my boss.

416
00:39:13,800 --> 00:39:16,280
Oab, he owns the bar where I work.

417
00:39:17,280 --> 00:39:18,840
Do you know him?

418
00:39:24,440 --> 00:39:27,520
Oab, I just came here to eat.

419
00:39:27,600 --> 00:39:30,520
I ran into a friend,
so we talked for a bit.

420
00:39:31,560 --> 00:39:35,120
Fon, what are you doing in Bangkok?

421
00:39:38,680 --> 00:39:39,920
Fon.

422
00:39:40,600 --> 00:39:43,080
Huh? What?

423
00:39:43,160 --> 00:39:44,640
What brought you to Bangkok?

424
00:39:46,880 --> 00:39:47,840
Oh.

425
00:39:49,760 --> 00:39:51,400
I was assigned to a new position here.

426
00:39:53,800 --> 00:39:56,560
You mean
you're a police officer, like Uncle Chai?

427
00:39:56,640 --> 00:39:57,760
Yes.

428
00:40:07,720 --> 00:40:11,720
Then I'll take Dom back.
The bar is really busy right now.

429
00:40:14,360 --> 00:40:15,720
Come on, Dom.

430
00:40:45,320 --> 00:40:46,280
You're a cop, right?

431
00:40:47,680 --> 00:40:48,600
No.

432
00:40:49,200 --> 00:40:51,520
Then why did you meet with a cop?

433
00:40:52,280 --> 00:40:53,120
We're friends.

434
00:41:02,160 --> 00:41:04,000
I told you, I'm not lying.

435
00:41:15,720 --> 00:41:17,480
How do you know her?

436
00:41:20,560 --> 00:41:21,440
We met at university.

437
00:41:22,440 --> 00:41:25,520
I was boxing there,
and Fon came to support a friend.

438
00:41:26,120 --> 00:41:27,520
That's how we met.

439
00:41:33,480 --> 00:41:34,600
That's all?

440
00:41:36,520 --> 00:41:37,520
Yes.

441
00:41:43,280 --> 00:41:44,560
We should get rid of him.

442
00:41:45,760 --> 00:41:46,760
I don't trust him.

443
00:41:49,040 --> 00:41:50,520
He met with a cop.

444
00:41:51,360 --> 00:41:53,120
Don't you think he's a mole?

445
00:41:59,200 --> 00:42:01,000
Are you sure you're not the mole?

446
00:42:02,280 --> 00:42:04,560
Are you lying? Huh?

447
00:42:17,720 --> 00:42:21,040
NO SMOKING

448
00:42:21,120 --> 00:42:22,160
Take him to the car.

449
00:42:25,480 --> 00:42:26,320
What did you say?

450
00:42:28,160 --> 00:42:29,240
Take him to the car.

451
00:42:53,560 --> 00:42:54,640
Move!

452
00:43:21,800 --> 00:43:23,200
Are you close with Fon?

453
00:43:29,080 --> 00:43:30,360
Didn't you hear me?

454
00:43:30,440 --> 00:43:33,920
I heard you. We're not that close.

455
00:43:36,040 --> 00:43:37,800
Did you get her number?

456
00:43:39,160 --> 00:43:41,480
We hadn't really talked much,
then you showed up.

457
00:43:42,320 --> 00:43:44,240
So I didn't get her contact.

458
00:43:46,400 --> 00:43:48,080
-Stop the car.
-Huh?

459
00:43:48,160 --> 00:43:49,120
Stop!

460
00:44:22,880 --> 00:44:23,960
Fon.

461
00:44:27,600 --> 00:44:28,640
Fon!

462
00:44:52,880 --> 00:44:55,520
KING BOXING CAMP

463
00:45:14,520 --> 00:45:16,160
Fon is your ex, right?

464
00:45:18,760 --> 00:45:19,760
No.

465
00:45:22,840 --> 00:45:24,440
I never broke up with her.

466
00:45:28,800 --> 00:45:31,000
How do I get to see her again?

467
00:45:44,120 --> 00:45:45,440
-Fon!
-Dom.

468
00:45:48,680 --> 00:45:52,560
I can't tell you much.
I came because I didn't want you upset.

469
00:45:53,200 --> 00:45:54,840
Why did you say we were just friends?

470
00:45:54,920 --> 00:45:56,400
I could only tell them that.

471
00:45:58,440 --> 00:45:59,840
What happened to you?

472
00:45:59,920 --> 00:46:01,320
It's a long story.

473
00:46:02,840 --> 00:46:04,440
Can you at least tell me where you are?

474
00:46:05,040 --> 00:46:05,920
I can't.

475
00:46:06,720 --> 00:46:08,560
Dom, you know
you're acting suspicious, right?

476
00:46:08,640 --> 00:46:09,680
I know.

477
00:46:10,200 --> 00:46:12,320
I just want you to know
I haven't done anything wrong.

478
00:46:12,400 --> 00:46:14,920
Everything I'm doing
is because I love you.

479
00:46:16,400 --> 00:46:18,040
-Are we going to see--
-I have to go.

480
00:46:18,920 --> 00:46:19,960
Dom.

481
00:46:44,760 --> 00:46:46,080
Hello, Boss.

482
00:46:48,840 --> 00:46:50,400
I haven't seen you in a while.

483
00:46:55,800 --> 00:47:00,160
When Liang came to see me the other day,
I took care of it.

484
00:47:00,760 --> 00:47:01,840
They should be heading out today.

485
00:47:01,920 --> 00:47:04,000
I don't want this kind of thing
to bring us shame.

486
00:47:04,520 --> 00:47:05,520
Yes.

487
00:47:06,200 --> 00:47:09,000
One rotten fish
can make the whole basket stink.

488
00:47:31,600 --> 00:47:32,920
Why are you spacing out?

489
00:47:33,560 --> 00:47:34,400
What's wrong?

490
00:47:36,880 --> 00:47:40,880
You said you never broke up with her,
but you haven't contacted her for years.

491
00:47:42,800 --> 00:47:43,840
Didn't you think
she might be married by now?

492
00:47:47,720 --> 00:47:49,760
-I did.
-Then why didn't you contact her?

493
00:47:52,320 --> 00:47:54,000
I wasn't ready.

494
00:47:57,360 --> 00:47:58,840
And now you are?

495
00:48:01,800 --> 00:48:02,960
No.

496
00:48:03,880 --> 00:48:05,440
If you're still not ready

497
00:48:05,520 --> 00:48:08,200
after getting this far, when will you be?

498
00:48:17,360 --> 00:48:18,440
That's the question.

499
00:48:21,040 --> 00:48:22,080
When will I be ready?

500
00:48:28,200 --> 00:48:29,400
Sorry, guys.

501
00:48:46,720 --> 00:48:47,960
WORLD BOXING

502
00:49:13,440 --> 00:49:15,320
Why is he staring at you?

503
00:49:17,240 --> 00:49:18,720
Probably doesn't like me.

504
00:49:18,800 --> 00:49:19,800
Huh?

505
00:49:25,360 --> 00:49:26,360
Hey.

506
00:49:26,440 --> 00:49:27,360
Yeah?

507
00:49:27,880 --> 00:49:29,160
What does Pong do here?

508
00:49:36,800 --> 00:49:37,800
It's all here.

509
00:49:47,560 --> 00:49:48,680
-Dum.
-Yeah?

510
00:49:49,200 --> 00:49:51,800
Can you take those two
to get something to eat for me?

511
00:49:55,880 --> 00:49:56,760
Sure.

512
00:50:00,040 --> 00:50:01,920
Hey, you two. Let's go eat.

513
00:50:02,720 --> 00:50:03,800
It's on me.

514
00:50:04,800 --> 00:50:06,320
Come on. What do you want to eat?

515
00:50:10,960 --> 00:50:12,480
Where did they get all that money?

516
00:50:13,120 --> 00:50:15,000
Did you see those stacks of cash
they gave Pong?

517
00:50:15,080 --> 00:50:16,080
Yeah.

518
00:50:23,160 --> 00:50:24,400
Look at that.

519
00:50:25,480 --> 00:50:27,160
Where did the fighters from the camp go?

520
00:50:27,760 --> 00:50:29,920
Hey, are you sure
they're not selling drugs?

521
00:50:30,520 --> 00:50:32,600
-Well, I--
-We're not selling drugs.

522
00:50:32,680 --> 00:50:34,480
They went to collect debts.

523
00:50:36,480 --> 00:50:37,560
-Collect debts?
-Yeah.

524
00:50:37,640 --> 00:50:39,400
We lend money.

525
00:50:39,480 --> 00:50:43,680
Some people pay us back on time.
Others keep dragging it out.

526
00:50:44,200 --> 00:50:45,880
If they can pay but won't, we have to…

527
00:50:45,960 --> 00:50:47,600
Send the fighters to collect it?

528
00:50:47,680 --> 00:50:48,480
Yeah.

529
00:50:50,520 --> 00:50:51,880
-Hey, Dum.
-Yeah?

530
00:50:51,960 --> 00:50:53,440
So would they send me too?

531
00:50:54,920 --> 00:50:56,760
-Send you?
-Yeah.

532
00:50:56,840 --> 00:50:59,200
The debtors would beat you up
and send you back.

533
00:50:59,280 --> 00:51:00,480
-What?
-Trust me.

534
00:51:00,560 --> 00:51:02,680
Save your strength for eating. Let's go.

535
00:51:02,760 --> 00:51:03,840
-Come on.
-Dum!

536
00:51:03,920 --> 00:51:04,840
Let's eat.

537
00:51:04,920 --> 00:51:06,000
No chance for me?

538
00:51:07,200 --> 00:51:08,200
Whoa, Dum!

539
00:51:09,520 --> 00:51:10,520
Come on.

540
00:51:13,200 --> 00:51:14,480
SOI SUAN

541
00:51:15,680 --> 00:51:16,800
It's from Aunt Pen.

542
00:51:20,240 --> 00:51:21,080
Hello?

543
00:51:23,960 --> 00:51:24,800
What?

544
00:51:26,600 --> 00:51:27,720
I'll be right there.

545
00:51:34,920 --> 00:51:36,840
-Here you go.
-Oh, here it is.

546
00:51:36,920 --> 00:51:38,760
I made it with all my heart.

547
00:51:38,840 --> 00:51:42,480
Let's see if it's still the same. Oh, wow!

548
00:51:43,320 --> 00:51:44,520
Is it good?

549
00:51:45,480 --> 00:51:48,120
-Same as always.
-You're so sweet.

550
00:51:48,720 --> 00:51:49,480
Bland as always.

551
00:51:50,240 --> 00:51:52,320
Want some seasoning? Here's salt.

552
00:51:53,640 --> 00:51:54,720
Something came up!

553
00:51:55,480 --> 00:51:56,960
You two, hurry up and come with me.

554
00:51:57,640 --> 00:51:59,600
Go on! Quick.

555
00:52:01,840 --> 00:52:03,080
-Auntie!
-Yeah?

556
00:52:03,160 --> 00:52:04,000
Keep the change.

557
00:52:05,960 --> 00:52:07,120
That's a lot.

558
00:52:08,920 --> 00:52:09,880
Hey!

559
00:52:10,400 --> 00:52:11,520
You didn't give me enough!

560
00:52:11,600 --> 00:52:15,040
Where are you rushing off to?
Is your dad in the ICU or something?

561
00:52:18,840 --> 00:52:20,640
We pay them every month, don't we?

562
00:52:21,240 --> 00:52:22,240
I know.

563
00:52:22,920 --> 00:52:24,440
Then why are they raiding our place?

564
00:52:24,520 --> 00:52:28,040
Someone tipped them off
that we were selling untaxed alcohol.

565
00:52:30,960 --> 00:52:31,960
Wait a second.

566
00:52:33,840 --> 00:52:36,360
Dum, the officers said
they're taking everything.

567
00:52:36,440 --> 00:52:39,280
Obviously. They were gonna take it anyway.

568
00:52:39,360 --> 00:52:42,160
So what now?
We'll settle it under the table later?

569
00:52:42,240 --> 00:52:43,760
Under the table, my ass.

570
00:52:43,840 --> 00:52:44,720
What?

571
00:52:46,080 --> 00:52:49,440
So they're really taking it all?
But we pay them every month.

572
00:52:56,480 --> 00:52:57,440
What do you think?

573
00:53:04,640 --> 00:53:05,920
Boss, their bar got hit.

574
00:53:07,200 --> 00:53:09,840
Good. I'll keep coming after them.

575
00:53:11,320 --> 00:53:14,240
Let's see how long they can last.

576
00:53:14,320 --> 00:53:16,200
Not only do they refuse to back down,

577
00:53:17,280 --> 00:53:20,840
they keep pissing me off.
I'll back them into a corner.

578
00:53:21,840 --> 00:53:23,440
Take them all out.

579
00:53:24,120 --> 00:53:25,520
POLICE REPORT

580
00:53:27,480 --> 00:53:28,840
Thirty days? Seriously?

581
00:53:28,920 --> 00:53:29,800
Yeah.

582
00:53:30,600 --> 00:53:32,480
They also get their liquor
from the same source.

583
00:53:46,680 --> 00:53:49,960
Hello, Sing. I need to order some liquor.

584
00:53:50,560 --> 00:53:52,760
I don't have any, Oab.
Nothing's come in yet.

585
00:53:54,320 --> 00:53:55,520
Really?

586
00:53:56,680 --> 00:53:59,400
When will the shipment arrive?
I'll place my order ahead of time.

587
00:54:00,080 --> 00:54:01,840
I really can't sell to you anymore.

588
00:54:01,920 --> 00:54:04,320
<i>Peng called me himself today.</i>

589
00:54:09,920 --> 00:54:11,760
That bastard Peng
told him not to sell to us.

590
00:54:12,360 --> 00:54:13,480
Damn it!

591
00:54:14,000 --> 00:54:15,760
Is there really nothing we can do?

592
00:54:15,840 --> 00:54:17,480
I want to make a move too.

593
00:54:17,560 --> 00:54:19,320
I want to kill that bastard.

594
00:54:25,160 --> 00:54:26,400
He's got too many men.

595
00:54:33,520 --> 00:54:34,840
Thank you all for coming.

596
00:54:34,920 --> 00:54:38,680
Everyone here is like family.
We care for each other.

597
00:54:39,280 --> 00:54:42,480
We stand together. We help each other.

598
00:54:44,040 --> 00:54:45,480
We watch each other's backs.

599
00:54:45,560 --> 00:54:50,000
Our unity is what makes us untouchable.

600
00:54:50,760 --> 00:54:53,840
If anyone here thinks about betraying us,

601
00:54:56,880 --> 00:54:59,360
they become an enemy of all of us.

602
00:55:03,160 --> 00:55:04,160
Cheers.

603
00:55:06,960 --> 00:55:08,280
You all know that, don't you?

604
00:55:09,160 --> 00:55:10,200
Yeah.

605
00:55:10,920 --> 00:55:11,920
Hey.

606
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:13,720
They're all shutting us out.

607
00:55:14,840 --> 00:55:16,720
Are we just going to let them do that?

608
00:55:17,720 --> 00:55:18,640
Calm down, Dum.

609
00:55:20,680 --> 00:55:21,960
I'll take them down.

610
00:55:24,200 --> 00:55:25,600
We just have to wait.

611
00:55:32,120 --> 00:55:34,960
Guys, come here.
I'll tell you everything at once.

612
00:55:35,560 --> 00:55:37,560
Think about it, everyone.

613
00:55:37,640 --> 00:55:41,680
Is there any place around here
that actually sells taxed liquor?

614
00:55:41,760 --> 00:55:44,720
It's like
they're slapping Oab in the face.

615
00:55:45,400 --> 00:55:47,240
Hey.

616
00:55:48,160 --> 00:55:50,760
I want you all
to go to bars in other areas.

617
00:55:51,640 --> 00:55:53,400
I want new liquor suppliers.

618
00:55:54,080 --> 00:55:55,240
-Yes, Boss.
-Go it.

619
00:56:05,360 --> 00:56:06,680
They're new. Take care of them.

620
00:56:06,760 --> 00:56:08,080
Sure. I'll handle it.

621
00:56:09,680 --> 00:56:11,160
Come on, you two.

622
00:56:11,840 --> 00:56:14,960
Let's go!
Why are you just standing there? Hurry up!

623
00:56:35,160 --> 00:56:37,400
-Is it done?
-Done, Boss.

624
00:56:39,120 --> 00:56:42,640
The more I sell,
the more you get your share.

625
00:56:47,440 --> 00:56:49,840
A lot of my stuff
got seized the other day.

626
00:56:51,440 --> 00:56:53,440
I can't give you a cut this time, Liang.

627
00:56:56,640 --> 00:57:00,000
Next time, if you're not around,
I won't send the goods.

628
00:57:02,560 --> 00:57:03,680
Yes.

629
00:57:06,320 --> 00:57:08,840
Oab and his guys
will probably need a new liquor supplier.

630
00:57:09,480 --> 00:57:11,760
I don't think
they'll look in their own area.

631
00:57:11,840 --> 00:57:15,680
If they step into our territory,
teach them a lesson.

632
00:57:15,760 --> 00:57:17,560
No matter where they go,

633
00:57:18,960 --> 00:57:20,600
it has to be my people.

634
00:57:23,040 --> 00:57:24,840
I had someone look into your background.

635
00:57:26,560 --> 00:57:29,080
-Your wife died?
-Yes.

636
00:57:29,160 --> 00:57:30,680
Your record says you don't have a wife.

637
00:57:34,080 --> 00:57:35,800
You guys are moving in on my territory.

638
00:57:36,680 --> 00:57:38,720
Boss said to take care of you

639
00:57:38,800 --> 00:57:40,200
if we find you.

640
00:57:47,640 --> 00:57:49,440
<i>You never contacted me.</i>

641
00:57:49,520 --> 00:57:52,280
I didn't want you to see me like that.

642
00:57:52,360 --> 00:57:53,240
It was embarrassing.

643
00:57:53,320 --> 00:57:56,040
<i>I wanted you to see</i>
<i>that you could rely on me.</i>

644
00:58:01,160 --> 00:58:02,640
Come here!

645
00:58:06,960 --> 00:58:07,960
Don't!

646
00:58:08,480 --> 00:58:10,040
This body is my relative.

647
00:58:42,600 --> 00:58:44,200
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
